<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Two overlapping bells.

  One bell says "alarm". Two, offset and split by a gap, say "a set of them",
  which is the product. Two shapes state plurality faster than any detail
  inside a single shape, and detail is the first thing to die at 48dp.

  Source of truth: logos/iterations/iteration-1.svg. That file is the design;
  this one is a mechanical transcription of its two paths. The viewport is kept
  at 512 to match the SVG exactly, so no coordinate has to be rescaled and no
  arc flag can be corrupted on the way in. android:width/height still place the
  mark on the standard 108dp adaptive-icon canvas.

  The gap between the bells is cut into the back bell's own outline, so it is
  unpainted background rather than a purple-filled shape. That matters because
  Android tints the monochrome themed icon one flat colour; a painted gap would
  disappear there and the two bells would merge into a blob.

  Safe zone: an adaptive icon is masked to a CIRCLE, not the bounding square.
  In this 512 viewport every painted point must sit within radius 156 of
  (256,256); the square's corners are ~221 out and would be clipped. The worst
  point here is the back bell's lower-left rim corner at 152.3, and the 13- and
  12-unit rim corner radii are what pull the corners inside - they are
  load-bearing, not decoration. Re-check this if the geometry is ever touched.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="512"
    android:viewportHeight="512">

    <!-- Back bell, with the separation cut into its own outline -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
        android:pathData="M 266.06 214.61 A 62 62 0 0 0 223 170.38 L 223 160 A 8 8 0 0 0 215 152 L 197 152 A 8 8 0 0 0 189 160 L 189 170.38 A 62 62 0 0 0 144 230 Q 144 277 122 312 L 122 325 A 13 13 0 0 0 135 338 L 228 338 L 228 332 Q 246 302 246 262 A 66 66 0 0 1 266.06 214.61 Z" />

    <!-- Front bell -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M 264 262 A 48 48 0 0 1 298 216.09 L 298 205 A 7 7 0 0 1 305 198 L 319 198 A 7 7 0 0 1 326 205 L 326 216.09 A 48 48 0 0 1 360 262 Q 360 302 378 332 L 378 340 A 12 12 0 0 1 366 352 L 258 352 A 12 12 0 0 1 246 340 L 246 332 Q 264 302 264 262 Z" />
</vector>
